        "original_id": "35bec270-1257-555d-9ba2-4436f7e17984",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lou Dials, Clarence Miles, Thomas D'Alesandro Jr., Peter Angelos\n- Organizations: Baltimore Orioles, Houston Astros, Cleveland Indians\n- Places: Baltimore, Maryland, St. Louis, Mexican League\n- Roles: scout, owner\n\nFacts:\n- From 1938 to 1941, Lou Dials played in the Mexican League.\n- After his playing career, Lou Dials became a scout for the Houston Astros, Cleveland Indians, and Baltimore Orioles.\n- In November 1953, a syndicate of Baltimore business and civic interests led by Clarence Miles and Mayor Thomas D'Alesandro Jr. purchased the Baltimore Orioles franchise after 52 years in St. Louis.\n- The Baltimore Orioles are an American professional baseball team based in Baltimore, Maryland.\n- Peter Angelos is the current majority owner of the Baltimore Orioles.",
